# Vir Kit

A modern, cross-framework UI component library built with **Vue 3** and **React**.

This project is a monorepo containing reusable components, shared styles, utilities, and tooling for building consistent user interfaces across different frontend frameworks.

[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](./LICENSE)
[![pnpm](https://img.shields.io/badge/pnpm-workspace-F69220)](https://pnpm.io/)
[![Turbo](https://img.shields.io/badge/Turborepo-enabled-EF4444)](https://turbo.build/)

---

## ✨ Features

- ⚛️ React component library
- 🟩 Vue 3 component library
- 🎨 Shared design tokens and styles
- 🌙 Theme support
- 📦 pnpm workspace monorepo
- ⚡ Turborepo build pipeline
- 🔥 TypeScript-first development
- 🧪 Vitest testing
- 📚 Storybook documentation
- 🧹 ESLint + Prettier
- 📝 Changesets changelog management
- 📄 MIT License

---

# 📦 Packages

| Package | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `@vir/react` | React UI components |
| `@vir/vue` | Vue 3 UI components |
| `@vir/styles` | Shared CSS variables, tokens, and themes |
| `@vir/utils` | Shared utility functions |

---

# 🏗 Repository Structure

```
vir-kit
│
├── packages
│   │
│   ├── react
│   │   ├── src
│   │   ├── stories
│   │   └── tests
│   │
│   ├── vue
│   │   ├── src
│   │   ├── stories
│   │   └── tests
│   │
│   ├── styles
│   │   └── design tokens
│   │
│   └── utils
│       └── shared helpers
│
├── .changeset
│
├── turbo.json
├── pnpm-workspace.yaml
├── tsconfig.json
├── eslint.config.js
├── .prettierrc
└── package.json
```

---

# 🚀 Getting Started

## Requirements

- Node.js >= 20
- pnpm >= 9

Check your versions:

```bash
node -v
pnpm -v
```

---

## Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-name/vir-kit.git

cd vir-kit
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
pnpm install
```

---

# Development

Run all packages:

```bash
pnpm dev
```

Run a specific package:

```bash
pnpm --filter @vir/react dev
```

or:

```bash
pnpm --filter @vir/vue dev
```

---

# Build

Build every package:

```bash
pnpm build
```

Build a single package:

```bash
pnpm --filter @vir/react build
```

---

# Testing

This project uses **Vitest**.

Run all tests:

```bash
pnpm test
```

Run tests with UI:

```bash
pnpm test:ui
```

Run package tests:

```bash
pnpm --filter @vir/react test
```

---

# Storybook

Storybook provides interactive component documentation.

## React Storybook

Start:

```bash
pnpm --filter @vir/react storybook
```

Open:

```
http://localhost:6006
```

---

## Vue Storybook

Start:

```bash
pnpm --filter @vir/vue storybook
```

Open:

```
http://localhost:6007
```

---

# Styling System

The shared styling package contains:

- CSS variables
- Design tokens
- Typography
- Colors
- Spacing
- Themes

Example:

```css
.button {
  background: var(--color-primary);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
}
```

Import styles:

```css
@import "@vir/styles";
```

---

# Component Development

A component should include:

```
Button
├── Button.tsx / Button.vue
├── Button.test.ts
├── Button.stories.ts
└── index.ts
```

Every component should provide:

- TypeScript types
- Tests
- Storybook documentation
- Accessibility support

---

# Adding Dependencies

Add a dependency to a package:

Example:

```bash
pnpm add lodash --filter @vir/utils
```

Add an internal package dependency:

```bash
pnpm add @vir/utils --filter @vir/react
```

Result:

```json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "@vir/utils": "workspace:*"
  }
}
```

---

# Code Quality

## Lint

Run ESLint:

```bash
pnpm lint
```

---

## Format

Run Prettier:

```bash
pnpm format
```

---

# Versioning & Changelog

This project uses **Changesets**.

Create a changeset:

```bash
pnpm changeset
```

Example:

```
@vir/react

minor

Added Button component
```

Update versions:

```bash
pnpm version
```

Publish packages:

```bash
pnpm release
```

---

# Publishing

Packages are published independently.

Example:

```bash
pnpm --filter @vir/react publish
```

Before publishing:

```bash
pnpm lint
pnpm test
pnpm build
```

---

# Design Goals

## Framework Agnostic

Vue and React components share:

- Same design language
- Same tokens
- Same accessibility principles

while keeping framework-specific APIs.

---

## TypeScript First

All packages provide:

- Strong typing
- Auto completion
- Type-safe APIs

---

## Accessibility

Components follow:

- Semantic HTML
- Keyboard navigation
- ARIA guidelines

---

# Contributing

Contributions are welcome.

## Development Flow

Create a branch:

```bash
git checkout -b feature/new-component
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
pnpm install
```

Develop:

```bash
pnpm dev
```

Run checks:

```bash
pnpm lint
pnpm test
pnpm build
```

Create a changeset:

```bash
pnpm changeset
```

Submit a pull request.

